  "type": "problem",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "description": "<div>\n  <p>A land square has four sides. Each side against water or beyond the map contributes one unit to the total coastline. Return the sum of all exposed land sides, including shorelines of separate islands.</p>\n  <p>Shared sides are internal, so they must not be counted twice.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid = [[1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 4</pre>\n  <p>Every side of the lone square is exposed.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid = [[1,1],[1,0]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 8</pre>\n  <p>The three-square L shape has eight exposed sides.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid = [[0,0],[0,0]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0</pre>\n  <p>Water contributes no sides.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= rows, columns &lt;= 100</code>; an empty grid has no islands.</li>\n    <li>All rows have equal length; cells have the values stated above.</li>\n    <li>Only side-sharing cells are adjacent; diagonal contact does not connect them.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
  "templates": {
    "python": "class Solution:\n    def islandPerimeter(self, grid: List[List[int]]):\n        \"\"\"NUMBER\"\"\"\n        pass\n",
    "javascript": "class Solution {\n  /** Return the required number result. */\n  islandPerimeter(grid) {\n    // your code here\n  }\n}\n"
  },
